35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The earlier works show a clear pattern of failure in hard surfaces.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the firms flagged clay subsoil. That explains the slippage risks.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The habitat fund only covers planting and water, not surfacing. That changes the math.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We have seven staff left, but two volunteer groups are active. That is a resource.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,The drainage callouts have doubled. The heat readings are also concerning.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"If the fund excludes buildings, we cannot rely on it for plazas.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"The depot notes say the south can be hoarded, but the center cannot.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that phasing constraint is critical. We need to keep the park open.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"The volunteer groups are good for habitat and sports, but not for general upkeep.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,People stick to firm ground. Soft margins are ignored during weekday crossings.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"So, hard surfaces are expensive to maintain and prone to failure.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,And the earth-moving is risky. We need a plan that works with the soil.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Planted ground costs triple to maintain, but the fund covers it. That is a trade-off.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We need a plan that the volunteers can actually support without burning out.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"The wetland plan addresses the drainage, but will people use it?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am leaning towards a plan that minimizes hard infrastructure.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. The woodland or wetland options seem more feasible given the soil.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"The wetland plan uses the fund effectively, but the maintenance is high.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"The woodland plan has lower maintenance needs than the wetland, I think.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"The wetland plan solves the drainage problem, which is our biggest issue.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
